Pyrobolic uses separately distributed upstream software, including Python,
PyGObject, GLib/Gio, GTK 4, libadwaita, GdkPixbuf, libsecret, python-xlib,
yt-dlp, FFmpeg and Deno. These components remain under their respective
upstream licenses. They are not relicensed by Pyrobolic's license.

The Debian package depends on distribution-provided libraries and tools.
Optional managed download support retrieves official yt-dlp and Deno releases;
yt-dlp's JavaScript challenge components (EJS) come from its official executable.
No third-party runtime binaries are embedded in this source tree or Debian package.

